MIT, and the reason is practical rather than philosophical: this repository
PRODUCES patches for llama.cpp, which is MIT. setup/patches/ holds one and
bench/reports/ holds an upstream comment. Apache-2.0's patent grant would buy
little here — what is in this repository is measured configuration, not a
patentable invention — and its terms would travel with any patch sent
upstream, which is friction in exactly the direction this work flows.

setup/patches/hip-integrated-off.patch is a diff against llama.cpp
(github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT). The context lines in it are llama.cpp's;
the change and the reasoning above it are this repository's.
